# DOC-research-series: Why the research paper series exists

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Paper ID** | `DOC-research-series` |
| **Subject document(s)** | `docs/research/` (RP-*, TP-*, DOC-*) |
| **Status** | `draft` |
| **Series** | Documentation system (`DOC-*`) |

## 1. Why this document exists

DESIGN leaves and TOOLS claims assert strong science cousins. Without written justification, architecture is assertion theater. Papers force problem, prior art, rationale, honesty mapping, acceptance criteria.

## 2. Problem statement

PM can mark not-started forever without explaining why a leaf is in DESIGN. Agents cannot prioritize vision vs residual. Conflicts stay implicit until product pain.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- Design rationale methods (IBIS/QOC).
- ADRs as lighter cousins. https://adr.github.io/
- Academic survey structure for related work.
- Living documentation — draft/accepted status avoids false finality.

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

RP = why in DESIGN; TP = why this process; DOC = why this control doc; CONFLICTS = fights + policy.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Drafts are not peer-reviewed journals. Citations need maintenance. Research must not override residual honesty.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

RP and TP drafts landed; DOC series lands with this paper. Promotion to accepted is human.

## 8. Open questions

1. External PDF publish later?
2. Require accepted research before PM done on vision leaves?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every DESIGN leaf has RP.
- [ ] TOOLS non-obvious claims have TP.
- [ ] Control docs have DOC.
- [ ] CONFLICTS kept current.

## 10. References

1. https://adr.github.io/
2. https://www.infoq.com/articles/book-review-living-documentation/
3. docs/research/README.oot

